Third-party material
--------------------
Catch Me Up bundles no third-party code, fonts or datasets. It uses only the Python standard
library.

- The idea of a skill that reads several platforms for a topic and a time window, then hands back
  the posts worth seeing, comes from the doomscroll skill by Jason Zhou (@jasonzhou1993) and
  Superdesign (https://github.com/superdesigndev/treg, Apache License 2.0 with additional terms).
  Catch Me Up is a from-scratch build and includes none of its code or text. It does not use the
  treg service. See "Credits" in README.md.
- Catch Me Up reads public pages and feeds from Hacker News (Algolia search), YouTube, Bluesky,
  Google News, GitHub, Mastodon, Product Hunt and Reddit. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  any of them, or by Anthropic. Their names appear only to say where posts come from. Each
  service's own terms apply to how you use what you read there.
